# OMS session memory (ContainerDoor)

Read these rules before changing OMS freight dashboard / email / sync:

| Topic | Rule file |
|-------|-----------|
| Activity Log + email queue/cron | `.cursor/rules/oms-activity-log.mdc` |
| Nav avatar + queue chip | `.cursor/rules/oms-nav-user.mdc` |
| EDD → Shopify sync | `.cursor/rules/oms-edd-shopify-sync.mdc` |
| Order amendments | `.cursor/rules/oms-order-amendments.mdc` |

---

## Status fields — no generic “Status”
- Primary customer-facing status = **`customerStatus`** (Confirmed / Dispatched / Delivered / Cancelled).
- Also: `warehouseStatus`, `paymentStatus`, `dispatchStatus`, `deliveryStatus`.
- There is **no** separate generic `status` DB column.
- Monday maps `customerStatus` → board column titled **"Status"** in code (`monday.server.ts`); prefer renaming that Monday title to **Customer Status** when touching Monday sync — do not invent a second OMS status field.

## Notes & Monday / Cin7 / Shopify
- Internal notes: OMS `CommunicationLog` only unless staff ticks sync checkboxes.
- ☐ **Send to Monday.com** — only checked notes create Monday Updates.
- ☐ **Send to Cin7** — UI “Coming Soon” (API path exists); keep disabled until ready.
- ☐ **Add to Shopify order timeline** — opt-in only (Note modal + Bulk).
- Routine field updates (EDD, payment, tracking, supplier) **must not** create Monday/Shopify notes.
- Bulk Actions Monday checkbox defaults **unchecked** (opt-in).

## Activity Log UI
- Source of truth: `CommunicationLog` only (`NotesPanel`).
- Field-change types (`*_update`, `system_event`) are **stored in DB** but **hidden** in UI via `SHOW_FIELD_CHANGE_LOGS = false` in `NotesPanel.tsx`. Flip to `true` later for full audit UI.
- Visible now: internal notes, emails, monday/shopify/cin7 note sync rows.

## Customer email (operational, not marketing)
- OMS is central place for ops emails; enqueue → cron sends (Resend/SMTP). Not Shopify marketing.
- NoteModal **Customer email**: subject + body → `BulkEmailJob` + `BulkEmailRecipient` + pending log.
- EDD/Tracking notify: opt-in checkbox → enqueue only.
- **Vercel Hobby:** no minutely cron — `vercel.json` crons disabled.
- **AWS / PM2 (future):** `ecosystem.config.cjs`
  - `oms-web` — `react-router-serve ./build/server/index.js` (PORT 3000)
  - `oms-email-queue-cron` — `scripts/email-queue-cron.mjs`
  - After build: `pm2 start ecosystem.config.cjs` (or `--only oms-web`)
- Auto-email on every EDD/status change: **No** — opt-in only (client direction).

## Bulk updates
- Core launch requirement (container/pre-order ops): bulk EDD, payment, supplier, notes, notify.
- Keep improving bulk; do not defer basic bulk field updates.

## EDD → customer account
- OMS `eddDate` must sync to Shopify metafield `containerdoor_ops.edd_{variantId}` (awaited).
- Customer Account freight block also reads live OMS via `GET /api/order-status`.
- Internal notes do not sync to Shopify automatically.

## Order amendments (CS)
- Detail → Customer → **Amend** (full-screen panel).
- Done: contact, address, delivery instructions, soft cancel line/order + audit + Shopify/Monday where applicable.
- Not yet: variant swap (`orderEdit`), hard `orderCancel`, Cin7 address/void.
- Migration: `prisma/migrations/20260725140000_order_amendment_fields/` (`shippingAddress2`, `deliveryInstructions`).

## Detail page UX (`/app/order/:orderId`)
- Hide nav **search** on detail (meaningless there).
- One note entry: Activity panel **Note / email** (not duplicate top-bar Add note).
- Remove dead **Notify** top button (use Note / email → Customer email).
- Detail actions: Update EDD · Tracking · Sync.

## Dashboard filters UX
- Filters apply **on change** (no hide-on-apply).
- Active filter **chips** always visible when applied; chip ✕ removes one.
- Toggle: Filters / Hide filters; Done closes panel.

## Amend UI
- Full-screen panel (`.fo-amend-overlay` / `.fo-amend-screen`), 3-column desktop, no scroll on desktop.
